      <section class="section shell" id="workflow" aria-labelledby="workflow-title">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <h2 id="workflow-title">From a quiet identity to a coordinated launch.</h2>
          <p>Use the accounts you already run to back each other up, so you are not posting to each one by hand.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="steps">
          <article class="step">
            <div class="step-number">01 / Connect</div>
            <div class="step-icon" aria-hidden="true">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M10 13a5 5 0 0 0 7.5.5l3-3a5 5 0 0 0-7-7l-1.7 1.7M14 11a5 5 0 0 0-7.5-.5l-3 3a5 5 0 0 0 7 7l1.7-1.7"></path></svg>
            </div>
            <h3>Pair your accounts</h3>
            <p>Connect the accounts you manage through Amber, using NIP-46 remote signing.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="step">
            <div class="step-number">02 / Compose</div>
            <div class="step-icon" aria-hidden="true">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="M12 20h9M16.5 3.5a2.1 2.1 0 0 1 3 3L8 18l-4 1 1-4Z"></path></svg>
            </div>
            <h3>Write the post</h3>
            <p>Draft the note and attach media. Each account keeps its own style guide, so the AI assist can help without making everything sound the same.</p>
          </article>
          <article class="step">
            <div class="step-number">03 / Emanate</div>
            <div class="step-icon" aria-hidden="true">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><circle cx="5" cy="12" r="2"></circle><circle cx="19" cy="5" r="2"></circle><circle cx="19" cy="19" r="2"></circle><path d="m7 11 10-5M7 13l10 5"></path></svg>
            </div>
            <h3>Schedule and sign</h3>
            <p>Pick when it publishes, set random delays for the reposts, and sign once. Emanator sends everything at the right time.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section shell" aria-labelledby="control-title">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <h2 id="control-title">Automation with a clear chain of custody.</h2>
          <p>Built on how Nostr already works: your identity is portable, the relays are open, and you hold the signing keys.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-grid">
          <article class="feature-card wide">
            <span class="feature-tag">Publishing control</span>
            <h3>See every post and repost before it goes out.</h3>
            <p>One calendar shows what each account has queued across the month, so nothing publishes that you have not looked at.</p>
            <div class="feature-shot browser-frame">
              <div class="browser-bar" aria-hidden="true">
                <i></i><i></i><i></i>
                <span class="browser-url">emanator.cypherpunk.today/calendar</span>
              </div>
              <img src="/landing/shots/calendar-desktop.png" width="1276" height="829" alt="Emanator calendar for September 2026, with scheduled posts and reposts laid out day by day across every managed account">
            </div>
          </article>
          <article class="feature-card">
            <span class="feature-tag">Identity first</span>
            <h3>Your signer holds the keys.</h3>
            <p>Emanator asks your signer to approve each event over NIP-46. Your Nostr private key stays in Amber, where it belongs.</p>
            <div class="privacy-line">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 22s8-4 8-10V5l-8-3-8 3v7c0 6 8 10 8 10Z"></path><path d="m9 12 2 2 4-4"></path></svg>
              No nsec custody
            </div>
          </article>
          <article class="feature-card">
            <span class="feature-tag">Account-aware AI</span>
            <h3>Keep each account sounding like itself.</h3>
            <p>Give every account its own style guide. The AI drafts and edits in that voice, instead of flattening them all into one generic tone.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section shell" id="tour" aria-labelledby="tour-title">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <h2 id="tour-title">The whole workflow, on the web and your phone.</h2>
          <p>Draft, schedule, and keep an eye on replies from wherever you are. The interface follows your system light or dark theme.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="tour-grid">
          <figure class="tour-card">
            <div class="browser-frame">
              <div class="browser-bar" aria-hidden="true">
                <i></i><i></i><i></i>
                <span class="browser-url">emanator.cypherpunk.today/interactions</span>
